\section{Discussion}\label{sec:discussion}

\paragraph{Layer selection as researcher degree of freedom~\citep{gelman2013garden}.}
Our five-metric ablation (\cref{sec:layer-results}) shows crossing rate reverses the central finding via shallow-layer compression (\cref{app:cosine_volatility}), observed across both Llama and Qwen (\cref{tab:r18b_full_layer}). Random-label controls (\cref{app:random_cp}) confirm the disagreement requires genuine safety labels across both architectures; the crossing-rate geometric bias is Qwen-specific (retained on QwQ-32B, dissolved on R1-8B). Contribution~1 (layer bias) generalizes from geometry, cross-dataset (AdvBench volatility ratio $1.67\times$; \cref{app:cosine_volatility}), and split-half replication (\cref{app:split_half}); Contribution~2 (HS advantage) is sample-dependent. Our finding is directional---cosine compression systematically biases crossing-rate metrics toward early layers, producing predictable conclusion reversals---distinct from general probe sensitivity~\citep{belinkov2022probing}; that this can reverse modality comparison conclusions suggests published safety detection results may warrant re-examination. Threshold-based layers peak at L63/64~\citep{wollschlager2025geometry}; R1-32B \emph{residualized} selectivity is 3.0pp (\cref{app:control}), below the 5pp threshold~\citep{hewitt2019control}.\looseness=-1

\paragraph{Encoder-quality boundary.}
The HS advantage is significant against 384d MiniLM (cross-validated at 7--8B; exploratory at 32B) but attenuated against 1024d BGE-large (1/4 HB). PCA capacity matching preserves significance across all four models (+16.8 to +23.1pp); whether stronger encoders~\citep{wang2024e5mistral,boxo2025linear_probes} close the gap bounds these claims' shelf life.\looseness=-1

\paragraph{Guidance for future research.}
Converging evidence supports genuine safety representations, but causal validation via DAS~\citep{geiger2023causal}, ITI~\citep{li2024iti}, or circuit breakers~\citep{zou2024improving} is needed; under quadratic position control, only 2/4 models retain significant non-positional HS advantage (\cref{tab:position_quadratic}), so position mediation remains unexcluded. We propose a multi-metric audit: compute ${\geq}3$ metrics, flag disagreement, verify cosine volatility (\cref{app:cosine_volatility,app:deployment_operating_points}); if layers diverge by ${>}20\%$ of depth, treat conclusions as metric-dependent; if volatility ratio exceeds $1.5\times$, prefer the lower-volatility layer. A three-layer ensemble eliminates metric pre-selection entirely (all four models $p \leq 0.002$; \cref{tab:ensemble}).\looseness=-1

